1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:18,600
Every case so far followed one student. Reports and Analytics ask what the Graduate School knows about all students at once. Every number is computed from the records, not typed in.

2
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:26,800
Graduate School staff signs in.

3
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:50,000
Reports and Analytics is under Overview. Three filters sit on top: program, entry cohort, and period, by default the last twelve months. Below, six numbers answer the questions the office asks most.

4
00:00:50,399 --> 00:01:04,000
Take Behind schedule: the share of active students who are behind, against a target. It shows at once whether the Graduate School is on track.

5
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:18,000
Median days to decide shows how fast requests are decided, against the twelve months before. Every number comes from recorded events and updates as work happens.

6
00:01:18,599 --> 00:01:31,599
The first tab, Needs attention, asks what holds students back. Each bar is a cause; the longest affects the most students.

7
00:01:31,799 --> 00:01:42,899
Selecting a cause narrows the list below to the students affected, so no bar is just a number.

8
00:01:43,099 --> 00:02:01,599
Show all causes restores the full list, most delayed first: stage, main reason, days in stage, and the office that can move the student on. Download it as Excel or PDF with the same filters.

9
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:15,800
Where students get stuck counts students per lifecycle stage as on time, slow, or stuck, with the limits underneath.

10
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:31,100
Every count here is a button. Selecting one opens the real students behind it, each linked to its record, so no figure is taken on trust.

11
00:02:33,099 --> 00:02:46,500
Office speed shows which offices take longest to close requests, grouped by days waiting. The longest red bar marks the office to ask first.

12
00:02:48,599 --> 00:03:00,100
Records to fix lists research students with missing records, such as no adviser on file. A fixed record drops off the list.

13
00:03:02,199 --> 00:03:12,900
The detailed lists remain. Cohorts by stage counts students of each program and entry year at each stage.

14
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:24,000
Graduation candidates shows who can graduate, what is missing, and each student's place in a graduation batch.

15
00:03:26,099 --> 00:03:35,000
Overdue and pending lists each waiting task and request, longest first, and the office that must act.

16
00:03:37,099 --> 00:03:43,500
Defenses lists held and upcoming defenses, with panel and verdict.

17
00:03:45,599 --> 00:03:56,700
Registrar changes is the daily list of changes made here that the Registrar must apply in AIMS, each marked when sent.

18
00:04:01,199 --> 00:04:20,900
Every filter covers the whole page. Graduate School staff picks one program, and the six numbers and charts follow. So the Graduate School monitors many students at once, not record by record.
